  "activity": {
    "id": "act_vectors_projectile",
    "name": "Vectors & Two-Dimensional Projectile Motion",
    "description": "A hands-on AR lab in which learners first build intuition for vectors as objects with magnitude and direction, practice vector addition (tip-to-tail) and decomposition into components, then apply these tools to two-dimensional projectile motion. Learners discover the independence of horizontal and vertical motion, the 45-degree maximum-range result, and consolidate through targeting and sandbox exploration.",
    "language": "en",
    "workplace": "wp_vectors_projectile",
    "start": "step_intro_vectors",
    "actions": [
      {
        "id": "step_intro_vectors",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "dev_hololens",
        "location": "place_vector_workspace",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "What Is a Vector?",
          "description": "A single arrow floats above the workspace with its tail fixed at the origin. Grab its head and drag it around in 3D space \u2014 watch the magnitude (length) and direction (angles relative to the colored x, y, z axes) update in real time. A vector has both a size and a direction, unlike a scalar such as temperature or mass which has only a size. Walk around the arrow: your viewpoint changes but the vector itself does not. Say 'next' when ready."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_axes_lines",
              "poi": "axes_center"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_vector_arrow",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_single_vector",
              "poi": "tail"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_vector_arrow",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_magnitude_label",
              "poi": "head",
              "text": "Magnitude = 25.0 units"
            },
            {
              "target": "thing_vector_arrow",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_direction_label",
              "poi": "head",
              "text": "Direction: 37 deg from x-axis"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_vectors",
              "viewport": "actions"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "thing_vector_arrow",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_vectors"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_vector_addition",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "step_vector_addition",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_vector_addition",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "dev_hololens",
        "location": "place_vector_workspace",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Adding Vectors: Tip-to-Tail",
          "description": "Two vectors appear: blue starts at the origin, and green is placed tip-to-tail at the head of blue. The red resultant runs from the tail of blue to the head of green. Grab and reorient either the blue or green vector and watch the resultant follow. Now swap their order \u2014 lay blue on green instead \u2014 and confirm the resultant points to exactly the same place. Order does not matter in vector addition. Say 'next' to continue."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_vector_blue",
              "poi": "vector_origin"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_vector_green",
              "poi": "vector_origin"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_vector_resultant",
              "poi": "vector_origin"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_instruction_hint",
              "poi": "axes_center",
              "text": "Swap the order of blue and green \u2014 the red resultant is unchanged."
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_addition",
              "viewport": "actions"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "augmentation": "pred_vector_blue"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "augmentation": "pred_vector_green"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "augmentation": "pred_vector_resultant"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "augmentation": "pred_instruction_hint"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_addition"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "triggers": [
          {
            "mode": "click",
            "id": "step_vector_decomposition",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          },
          {
            "mode": "voice",
            "id": "step_vector_decomposition",
            "type": "action",
            "viewport": "actions",
            "operator": "equal"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "step_vector_decomposition",
        "viewport": "actions",
        "type": "actions",
        "device": "dev_hololens",
        "location": "place_vector_workspace",
        "instruction": {
          "title": "Decomposition: Addition in Reverse",
          "description": "A single vector appears. From the origin, three color-coded component arrows emerge tip-to-tail: x from the origin, then y from the tip of x, then z from the tip of y \u2014 ending exactly at the head of the original vector. Grab and resize each component along its axis; the original vector updates to remain the sum. Decomposition is just addition run backwards: the resultant broken into pieces that add back to it. In two dimensions the components and the magnitude form a right triangle (Pythagoras). Say 'next' to move to projectile motion."
        },
        "enter": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_single_vector",
              "poi": "vector_origin"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_component_x",
              "poi": "vector_origin"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_component_y",
              "poi": "vector_origin"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_component_z",
              "poi": "vector_origin"
            },
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_instruction_hint",
              "poi": "axes_center",
              "text": "Vx, Vy, Vz add tip-to-tail to reproduce V. |V| = sqrt(Vx^2 + Vy^2 + Vz^2)"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "type": "predicate",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_decomposition",
              "viewport": "actions"
            }
          ],
          "deactivate": [],
          "messages": [],
          "if_logic": []
        },
        "exit": {
          "remove_self": false,
          "activates": [],
          "deactivate": [
            {
              "target": "place_vector_workspace",
              "type": "*",
              "augmentation": "*"
            },
            {
              "target": "person_learner",
              "augmentation": "pred_narration_decomposition"
            }
          ],
          "messages": [],
